The \textbf{surprise test set} was drawn from a French literary works corpus not disclosed before submission, designed to probe out-of-domain generalisation.

\subsubsection{Label Distribution and Class Imbalance}

The label distribution is strongly skewed toward \texttt{FALSE} in both training and development data.
\texttt{isAt=TRUE} is rarest of all, since it requires evidence of a current or habitual connection rather than any past mention.
This imbalance means a system can achieve GMR of 0.4167 without learning anything meaningful; improving substantially beyond it requires correctly recalling the minority classes.
Figure~\ref{fig:labeldist} shows the label distributions in the development set.

